-- **Rules grouping** — Scenarios with a `Rule` property are grouped under a collapsible rule heading. Background step detection is scoped per-rule when rules are present.
-- **Examples / Scenario Outline tables** — Scenarios sharing an `OutlineId` are rendered as examples tables with parameter columns and per-row status icons. When an outline has multiple named `Examples:` blocks, a separator band carrying the block name, its optional description and a per-block pass/fail count is drawn between the row groups (3.0.64+; see [Named Examples blocks](#named-examples-blocks) below).
-- **Failure clustering** — Failed scenarios are grouped by the **first line of the error message** (with a Shouldly message's check from its second line; for one Shouldly wrote without its source, its check and expected value) — not by the stack trace, and not by similarity — and collapsed under one cluster heading. The report and `Failures.md` use the same key, so the two cannot disagree about which failures share a cause. Treat a cluster as a strong hint that one cause is behind all of them rather than a finding that one is: two unrelated assertions can open with the same line.
