-- **Database toggle** — When any diagram in the report contains a `database` or `collections` participant (from CosmosDB, EF Core, MongoDB, DynamoDB, Spanner, BigQuery, Redis, distributed caches, or any extension that renders as a database/collections shape), a **"Databases Shown" / "Databases Hidden"** toggle button appears in the toolbar. Clicking it hides all database and cache participants and their associated arrows, simplifying the diagram to show only service-to-service communication. The toggle works at both report level and scenario level. It applies only to scenario sequence diagrams — the embedded [component diagram](Component-Diagrams) is an architecture overview and is never affected by any of the filter toggles (3.0.82+; its database/collections dependency nodes always stay drawn). See [[Tracking Custom Dependencies]] for how participants are assigned the `database` or `collections` shape.
-- **Note JSON ⇄ YAML toggle** (browser-rendered reports, 3.0.59+) — Hovering a diagram note whose body is JSON shows a **`Y`** button that re-renders the payload as YAML, unfolding `\n` (and uniform `\r\n`) escapes in string values (SQL queries, stack traces) into literal block scalars with their original line breaks; **`J`** toggles back to the exact original JSON. Since 3.0.66 compact **JSON/YAML** dropdowns beside the filter toggles convert every eligible note at once — report-wide or per scenario — and reports start in YAML from 4.0.0; `ReportConfigurationOptions.NotePayloadFormat` (CLI: `kronikol ingest --note-format`) chooses the format a report starts in. See [[PlantUML Browser Rendering › Note Payload JSON ⇄ YAML Toggle (3.0.59+)|PlantUML-Browser-Rendering#note-payload-json--yaml-toggle-3059]].
