new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bf82945
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Migrating-to-v5-Report.md
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+## The report's tabs, themes and settings
+
+Kronikol 5.0.0 redraws the HTML report: a light and a dark theme on colour tokens, a run band in place of the header
+row, a filter box with rows of chips, and tabs where 4.x had toolbar toggles, panels and disclosures. A report opens as
+before and a 4.x link still works, but a stylesheet, a script or a browser test written against 4.x's markup may need
+changing, and some settings now mean something else.
+[[Generated Reports › Report Features|Generated-Reports#report-features]] describes the 5.0.0 report and
+[[Report Themes]] its tokens. Labels and categories, which became tags, have a page of their own:
+[[Migrating to v5: tags|Migrating-to-v5-Tags]]. [[Migrating to v5]] lists every 5.0.0 change, with the settings that
+keep the 4.x behaviour.
+
+### What changed
+
+| | 4.x | 5.0.0 |
+|---|---|---|
+| Colours | fixed colours on each rule, one theme | tokens (`--kron-*` for the page, `--dg-*` for its diagrams), each with a light and a dark value; the page follows the system's setting until the reader picks a theme with the switch at the right of the title |
+| The report's sections | Scenario Timeline and Component Diagram toolbar toggles, and History and Report diagnostics sections above the features | the Features, Timeline, Components, History and Diagnostics tabs of a report bar that pins to the top of the window on a desktop |
+| The run summary | a header row: the pie chart, the Test Execution Summary table and the CI table | the run band: the ring, the summary as labelled figures and the CI details, in one card |
+| The features table | the Features Summary disclosure above the run summary | the Summary view of the Features tab, beside the Full view of the feature cards |
+| Expand and collapse | Expand All buttons whose labels flipped | a pair of icon buttons for features and a pair for scenarios, dimmed while they have nothing to do |
+| Happy paths | a Happy Paths Only toggle | Show, Only or Hide |
+| The filter rows | always open on a desktop; OR/AND switches; a dependency button on or off | folded under More filters on a desktop; ANY/ALL switches; a chip goes off, has, has not |
+| A scenario's diagram toolbar | the view toggles and the payload controls on one bar | the views as tabs on a bar of their own, and the payload controls behind a gear |
+| Payload controls | the Details radio (Expand, Collapse, Truncate) and labels such as "Databases Shown" | Payloads (Expanded, Collapsed, Truncated), and toggles that say their word alone, with `aria-pressed` |
+| Start states | assertion notes hidden, payloads cut at 40 lines, the dependency filter on AND | every diagram toggle but Headers on, payloads cut at 10 lines, the dependency filter on ANY (OR) |
+| History in the report | none by default (the History section from 3.21.0, the rest from 4.6.0) | the History tab, on by default; each scenario's history still only with `ShowScenarioHistory` |
+| Diagnostics in the report | none by default (from 3.21.0) | the Diagnostics tab, on by default |
+| The labs page | no script, 4.x's colours | the report's theme, with the theme's two scripts |
+
+### Stylesheets
+
+- Every colour of the report is a token. Set the tokens in `CustomCss`: the light values on `:root`, the dark values
+  on `:root[data-theme="dark"]` and again on `:root:not([data-theme])` under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`
+  ([[Report Themes › Restyling a report with its tokens|Report-Themes#restyling-a-report-with-its-tokens]]).
+- A sheet written against 4.x's rules or colours may no longer apply where 5.0.0 changed the markup: the features and
+  their steps, the failure diff, the parameter table, the run band, the filter rows and the payload controls. Where
+  it still applies it paints the same colours in both themes, so its light colours stay on a dark page. Set the
+  tokens instead.
+- These classes are gone: `.header-row`, `.test-execution-summary`, `.summary-chart`, `.ci-chart-group` and
+  `.ci-metadata` (the run band replaced them); `.features-summary-details`; `.collapse-expand-all`; `.happy-path-toggle`
+  and `.happy-path-active`; and `svg.history-chart-svg` with `history-bar-pass`, `history-bar-fail`,
+  `history-bar-duration` and `history-bar-partial`: the pass rate is a ring per run now, and the duration trend is
+  drawn as HTML bars (`.history-bars`, `.history-bar`). The Categories row's classes went with the row
+  ([[Migrating to v5: tags › The report|Migrating-to-v5-Tags#the-report]]).
+- `.status-toggle`, `.percentile-btn`, `.dependency-toggle` and `.dep-mode-toggle` keep their names under new rules,
+  so a 4.x rule for them may no longer apply.
+- `Stylesheets.VioletThemeStyleSheet`, the Specifications report's default sheet, sets the colour tokens for the light
+  and the dark theme, and keeps 4.x's solid violet, with white on it, for a chosen control, the passed step and the
+  back-to-top button. A sheet built on the 4.x constant's rules sets the tokens instead
+  ([[Report Themes › The violet theme|Report-Themes#the-violet-theme]]).
+
+### Scripts and browser tests
+
+- These page functions are gone: `toggle_timeline` and `toggle_component_diagram` (click the tab,
+  `button.report-tab[data-tab="timeline"]` or `[data-tab="components"]`); `toggle_expand_collapse` (the
+  `button.fold-btn` pairs); `toggle_happy_paths` and `filter_happy_paths` (the `button.happy-seg` buttons);
+  `toggle_dependency` (the chips and switches answer one delegated handler, so click the chip); and
+  `toggle_examples_detail`, which every 4.x report carried and nothing in it called. `filter_categories`,
+  `toggle_cat_mode` and `toggle_category` went with the Categories row.
+- The timeline, the component diagram, the History section and the diagnostics are in tab panels that stay hidden
+  until their tab is chosen. A test that checks one of them is visible selects its tab first.
+- On a desktop the filter rows are folded under More filters, and the filter box carries `rows-folded` while they
+  are, so a test that uses a row's control presses `button.more-filters` first. The search field sits in
+  `span.search-field`.
+- A scenario's payload controls are behind its gear: `button.scenario-settings-gear` opens `div.scenario-settings`,
+  whose bar is `div.diagram-toggle.diagram-options-bar`, and the view tabs are `div.diagram-toggle.diagram-toggle-tabs`.
+  A section showing another view carries `diagrams-not-seq`, and a section with no sequence diagram has no payload
+  controls. On a phone, `button.scenario-diagram-controls-toggle.gear-in-summary` on the diagrams' title replaces
+  4.x's "Diagram Settings" button.
+- A toggle's label is its word alone (Headers, Assertions, Steps, Databases, Events, Setup), and its state is in
+  `aria-pressed` and `data-shown`: a test that looked for "Databases Shown" reads `aria-pressed`. Each label sits in
+  `span.btn-label`. The Details radio reads Payloads, and its line count shows only while Truncated is picked.
+- A filter row's switch reads ANY or ALL and keeps AND or OR in `data-mode`, which the link writes as before. A chip
+  carries `aria-pressed` (`true`, `mixed` or `false`) and `dependency-active` or `dependency-exclude`.
+- The CI details lose their colons (`Build #:` and `42` are `Build` and `#42`), and the hidden Kronikol Version row
+  is gone: the version is in the page's `generator` meta.
+- A note's buttons are named in `data-note-btn`; `truncate`, `truncate-bottom`, `collapse-bottom` and
+  `expand-bottom` are new.
+- Whenever the scenarios shown change, the page raises `kron-filter-change` on the document, with
+  `{ shown, total }` in its `detail`, which a test can wait for.
+
+### Settings
+
+- **`ReportToggleDefaults`**
+  ([[Report Configuration › Toggle Default Start States|Report-Configuration#toggle-default-start-states]]):
+  - `AssertionsShown` defaults to `true` (4.x: `false`), `TruncateLines` to `TruncateLineCount.Lines10` (4.x:
+    `Lines40`), and `DependencyFilterMode` to `FilterCombinationMode.Or` (4.x: `And`). Set the three back to open a
+    report as 4.x did.
+  - `ScenarioTimelineVisible` and `ComponentDiagramVisible` choose the tab the page opens on, the Timeline when both
+    are set, where they showed a panel.
+  - `FeaturesSummaryOpen` opens the Features tab on its Summary view, where it opened the Features Summary
+    disclosure.
+  - `FeaturesExpanded` and `ScenariosExpanded` still open the sections, and start the matching expand button dimmed,
+    where they seeded its label.
+  - `DiagnosticsOpen` has nothing left to open: the Diagnostics tab is always open.
+  - `EventsShown` and `SetupShown` are new, both `true` by default.
+  - `CategoryFilterMode` is `TagFilterMode`.
+- **`ShowHistorySection` and `ShowReportDiagnosticsSection`** default to `true` (`false` from 3.21.0 to 4.x): a run
+  that read history has a History tab, and one that recorded a diagnostic has a Diagnostics tab with their count on
+  it. `ShowScenarioHistory` stays `false`. Set the two to `false` for a report without the tabs; the labs page beside
+  the report carries both either way. `kronikol merge` renders with the defaults, so a merge given `--history` has a
+  History tab, and one whose shards recorded a diagnostic a Diagnostics tab.
+- **`kronikol ingest`** shows the Diagnostics tab by default. `--no-diagnostics-section` leaves it out, and
+  `--diagnostics-section` is still taken, so a 4.x command line runs unchanged.
+- **`ComponentDiagramOptions.Title`** heads the Components tab under every renderer, and the drawing leaves it out;
+  `ComponentDiagram.html` still draws it.
+
+### Links
+
+- A link copied from a 4.x report opens the same view, except one that chose dependencies and has no `depmode`: it
+  meant AND, and in a default 5.0.0 report it means OR. A report whose old links should keep AND sets
+  `DependencyFilterMode = FilterCombinationMode.And`, or a link can say `depmode=AND`.
+- `hp=1` still opens on happy paths Only, and a link that chose `(no interactions)` opens on No dependencies.
+- 5.0.0 adds `depx=`, `hpx=1`, `tags=`, `tagx=` and `tagmode=`. The display settings are not in the link: each load
+  starts them from the report's settings
+  ([[Generated Reports › Deep links|Generated-Reports#deep-links-scenario--and-sid-]]).
+
+### What a report shows differently
+
+- Assertion notes are drawn from the first render, and payloads are cut at 10 lines.
+- A service is drawn as a box: `DependencyPalette.GetSequenceShape(DependencyType.HttpApi)` returns `participant`, where
+  it returned `entity`. Databases are deep cyan, `#0E7C86` where they were `#E74C3C`, and `DependencyColors` still
+  overrides it. Where the page draws a diagram, a step bar is a flat band in the step colour (`--dg-step`) with its
+  label in bold, in place of the black hexagon.
+- The ring reads 100% only when every scenario passed (4.x rounded 213 passed of 214 up to 100%), and a scenario
+  skipped after an earlier failure counts as skipped in the summary and the ring.
+- The parameter table's rows are not tinted by their status, and the failure diff's labels read Expected and Actual,
+  without a colon.
+- A bypassed scenario's timeline bar is blue, as the ring draws it (orange in 4.x).
+- A scenario whose diagram makes no call has no dependency: it is under No dependencies.
+- A collapsed payload's one-line preview leaves out a JSON body's braces.
+- A duration of an hour or more reads in hours (`1h 5m`, where it read `65m 0s`).
+- A run whose calls give the component diagram no connection has no Components tab, where 4.x drew the title alone.
+- `Specifications.html` is dark and violet in the dark theme, and has the report bar, with the Features and Timeline
+  tabs, whenever its scenarios carry durations.
