@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Migrating to v5
+
+Kronikol 5.0.0 writes the run's data file as `TestRunReport.krkl`, redraws the HTML report with tabs, a light and a
+dark theme and new filters, replaces labels and categories with tags, and runs on .NET 10 alone. This page lists
+each change and the setting that keeps the 4.x behaviour where there is one; the report and the tags each have a page
+of their own with the detail. Upgrading from 3.x? Read [[Migrating to v4]] first.
+
+## What changed
+
+| | 4.x | 5.0.0 | To keep the 4.x behaviour |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| The run's data file | `TestRunReport.json` | `TestRunReport.krkl`: the same report, compressed whole | `CompressTestRunReport = false`, or `kronikol ingest --data-file json` |
+| The data file's schema | Written beside every report | Written only when asked | `GenerateTestRunReportSchema = true`, or `--schema` on `kronikol merge` and `kronikol ingest` |
+| Target frameworks | net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 | net10.0 | None: a test project on .NET 8 or 9 stays on 4.x |
+| `CompressTestRunReportPayloads` | On by default | Obsolete (warning CS0618), and reaches only the JSON file | Set it only alongside `CompressTestRunReport = false`; v6 removes it |
+| A closed composite step's sub-steps | Drawn in the page | Drawn the first time the step opens, where they come to 2 KB of HTML or more | `RenderCollapsedSubStepsOnExpand = false` |
+| The HTML report | Toolbar toggles, panels and disclosures, one set of colours | Tabs on a report bar, a light and a dark theme on colour tokens, a run band, filter rows folded under More filters | None: a stylesheet, a script or a browser test written against 4.x's markup may need changing ([[Migrating to v5: the report|Migrating-to-v5-Report]]) |
+| Start states | Assertion notes hidden, payloads cut at 40 lines, the dependency filter on AND | Every diagram toggle but Headers on, payloads cut at 10 lines, the dependency filter on ANY (OR) | `AssertionsShown = false`, `TruncateLines = TruncateLineCount.Lines40` and `DependencyFilterMode = FilterCombinationMode.And` on `TestRunReportToggleDefaults` (and `SpecificationsToggleDefaults`) |
+| History and diagnostics in the report | Left out by default (on the labs page from 4.6.0) | The History and Diagnostics tabs, on by default | `ShowHistorySection = false` and `ShowReportDiagnosticsSection = false`, or `kronikol ingest --no-diagnostics-section` |
+| Labels and categories | `Feature.Labels`; `Scenario.Labels` and `Scenario.Categories` | `Feature.Tags` and `Scenario.Tags`, filled by every adapter from its framework's own tagging | None: the members are gone, and code that used them moves to tags ([[Migrating to v5: tags|Migrating-to-v5-Tags]]) |
+
+```csharp
+var options = new ReportConfigurationOptions
+{
+    CompressTestRunReport = false,             // TestRunReport.json, as 4.x wrote it
+    GenerateTestRunReportSchema = true,        // TestRunReport.schema.json beside it
+    RenderCollapsedSubStepsOnExpand = false,   // every step drawn in the page
+    ShowHistorySection = false,                // no History tab
+    ShowReportDiagnosticsSection = false,      // no Diagnostics tab
+    TestRunReportToggleDefaults = new ReportToggleDefaults
+    {
+        AssertionsShown = false,                          // assertion notes hidden
+        TruncateLines = TruncateLineCount.Lines40,        // payloads cut at 40 lines
+        DependencyFilterMode = FilterCombinationMode.And, // the dependency filter on AND
+    },
+};
+```
+
+
+## The data file is `TestRunReport.krkl`
+
+A run writes `TestRunReport.krkl` in place of `TestRunReport.json`. It is the same report as compact JSON, without the
+keys that hold nothing (unless the schema requires them), with every payload as text, and the whole compressed with
+zstd. It declares `formatVersion` 3. On BreakfastProvider's LightBDD report the JSON was 6,150,370 bytes and the
+`.krkl` 279,968, about a twentieth; a report filled by large payloads shrinks less, since each payload is already
+most of its own size. A mergeable run (`GenerateMergeableData`) writes its mergeable file the same way.
+
+What reads it:
+
+- **`kronikol` 4.30.0 and later**: every `kronikol query` verb, `kronikol merge`, `kronikol diff` and the rest. An older
+  `kronikol` refuses the file rather than half-reading it. Update the tool: `dotnet tool update -g Kronikol.Tool`.
+- **The `query.cs` beside the report** reads it, with nothing installed.
+- **`query.py`** reads it on Python 3.14 or later, which can decompress zstd; on an older Python it says so and stops.
+- **The history action.** The tool its `VERSION` file installs reads `.krkl`, so a workflow that pins the action to
+  a tag before `v4.30.0` has to move it on.
+- **Your own scripts.** The file is not JSON on disk, so `jq`, a `grep` or a JSON parser reads nothing from it.
+  `kronikol decode TestRunReport.krkl -o TestRunReport.json` writes the JSON, and `--indent` indents it; or set
+  `CompressTestRunReport = false` and keep the JSON. To answer a question about a run, `kronikol query` never needs
+  the JSON.
+- **CI uploads.** An artifact step that names `TestRunReport.json` finds nothing: name `TestRunReport.krkl`, or upload
+  the reports folder. See [[CI Artifact Upload]].
+- **Kronikol4J** writes its own file and is not affected.
+
+`CompressTestRunReportPayloads` has no effect on a `.krkl`: the payloads are text inside a file compressed whole, which
+comes out smaller than payloads compressed one by one.
+
+## The schema is written only when asked
+
+`GenerateTestRunReportSchema` defaults to `false`, so a run no longer writes `TestRunReport.schema.json` beside its
+report. Nothing in Kronikol reads it. Set the option to `true`, or pass `--schema` to `kronikol merge` or
+`kronikol ingest`, if something of yours validates the data file or the JSON `kronikol decode` writes. A schema an
+earlier run left at the top of the reports folder stays there, since no `Run.json` lists it.
+
+## .NET 10 alone
+
+Every package targets net10.0 alone; net8.0 and net9.0 are dropped, and net11.0 joins in a 5.x release when .NET 11
+ships. A test project on .NET 8 or 9 stays on 4.x. The project templates offer `--Framework net10.0` alone.
+
+## `CompressTestRunReportPayloads` is obsolete
+
+It still works where it did, on the JSON file a run writes with `CompressTestRunReport = false`, and v6 removes it.
+Code that sets it gets warning CS0618 when it builds, which fails a build that treats warnings as errors: delete the
+line, unless you keep the JSON file and want its payloads compressed. `kronikol ingest --payloads` is obsolete with it.
+
+## Sub-steps are drawn when their step first opens
+
+A composite step is drawn closed, as in 4.x. Where its sub-steps come to 2 KB of HTML or more, the page now holds them
+compressed and draws them the first time the step is opened, so a suite of deeply nested steps (LightBDD composites
+20 levels down, say) keeps a small report. A step on the way to a failure is drawn and open as before. The report's
+search box finds a word in a step nobody opened, Export Filtered HTML carries the steps its scenarios need, and a row
+of a parameterized group opens the steps that were open in the row it replaced.
+
+The browser's own find (Ctrl+F) cannot see a step nobody opened, and neither can a script or a test of yours that
+looks for a sub-step's markup in the page's HTML. Set `RenderCollapsedSubStepsOnExpand = false` to draw every step in
+the page.
+
+## `kronikol ingest` and `kronikol merge`
+
+`kronikol ingest` follows the library: without flags it writes `TestRunReport.krkl` and no schema.
+`--data-file json` writes the JSON, `--schema` the schema, and `--payloads` applies only with `--data-file json`.
+`kronikol merge` writes a `.krkl` when any input is one or `-o` names that extension, so shards from 5.0.0 runs merge
+into a `.krkl`; `--schema` writes the schema beside the merged file. See [[Ingesting External Captures]] and
+[[Merging Parallel Reports]].
+
+## The report
+
+[[Migrating to v5: the report|Migrating-to-v5-Report]] covers the report's tabs, themes and settings: the stylesheet
+classes and page functions that are gone or changed, what a browser test should select now, the settings that mean
+something new, the links, and what a report shows differently. [[Report Themes]] lists the colour tokens.
+
+## Tags
+
+[[Migrating to v5: tags|Migrating-to-v5-Tags]] covers labels and categories becoming tags: the members that are
+gone, what each adapter reads, how a 4.x data file and a 4.x tool read a 5.0.0 one, and what the report's Tags row
+shows.
