 ### Semantics worth knowing
 
 - **Defaults govern the initial state only.** After any interaction the page state is whatever the interaction leaves, exactly as with the built-ins. Search still collapses non-matching scenarios and force-opens a single match (including its steps and diagrams sections, and an enclosing rule, if a configured default closed them); *Clear All* does not restore `open` states. There is no "return to configured defaults" button.
-- **Zero-click rendering follows the seed.** The configured state drives the render pipeline itself, not just the buttons — an `AssertionsShown = true` report draws assertion notes on first paint.
-- **URL-hash grammar** (changes even for non-adopters, 3.0.80): the hash omits `depmode`/`tagmode` when the mode equals the *configured* default (previously the built-in), and `parse_url_hash` now accepts both values symmetrically — `depmode=AND` and `tagmode=OR`, previously ignored, are valid, so a deep link from an AND-default report forces AND on an OR-default report. Before 5.0.0 the category filter's mode was `catmode`; a link that carries it, and no `tagmode`, sets the tag mode. *Clear All* resets the modes to the configured defaults, never to hard-coded AND/OR. Since 3.1.0 a `#scenario-`/`#sid-` anchor may lead the hash (`#sid-<id>&status=Failed`); filter rewrites and *Clear All* both preserve it — see [Generated Reports › Deep links](Generated-Reports#deep-links-scenario--and-sid-).
-- **Deep search vs seeded-hidden diagram content:** the search index is generation-time and state-independent, so a hit can land on content a seeded state strips from the rendered diagram (e.g. database notes with `DatabasesShown = false`) — the same class of behaviour assertions have always had (hidden by default, still searchable). The toggle that re-reveals the content is the one named by the setting.
