@@ -0,0 +1,202 @@
+# Report Themes
+
+A report opens in a light or a dark theme (5.0.0). Every colour it draws comes from a set of CSS custom properties,
+its tokens, so a stylesheet of your own can restyle it by setting them again.
+
+## Light and dark
+
+A report follows the system's light or dark setting, and keeps following it as it changes, until the reader picks a
+theme with the switch at the right of the report's title. The pick then holds, over a reload and over the system's
+setting. The theme is chosen in the page's head, before anything is drawn, so the page never flashes the other theme.
+
+The pick is the one thing a report keeps in the browser: it is stored in local storage as `kronikol.theme`. Where the
+browser refuses the page its storage, the pick holds while the page is open, over the system's setting too, and the
+next load follows the system's setting again.
+
+Only the filters live in the page's link: the search (`q`), `status`, `deps`, `depx`, `depmode`, `hp`, `hpx`, `tags`,
+`tagx`, `tagmode`, `dur` and `pctl`
+([[Generated Reports › Deep links|Generated-Reports#deep-links-scenario--and-sid-]]), beside a scenario's address,
+which opens the Features tab. Nothing else is kept: the display toggles, the payload controls, the tab and what is
+open start from the report's settings on each load
+([[Report Configuration › Toggle Default Start States|Report-Configuration#toggle-default-start-states]]).
+
+A copy of the page opened without its scripts still follows the system's setting, through a
+`prefers-color-scheme` block in the token sheet.
+
+The labs page (`TestRunReport.labs.html`) and the Specifications report take the theme the same way, with the same
+switch on their title line.
+
+## Diagrams
+
+The page draws a diagram in the theme's colours: participants, arrows, notes, step bars, lanes and labels read their
+colours from the `--dg-*` tokens. A copy of a diagram (the right-click menu's Copy, Save and Open in new tab, as SVG
+or PNG) carries the look in the light theme's colours, whichever theme the page shows, so a pasted diagram reads on a
+white document.
+
+## Restyling a report with its tokens
+
+Set the tokens again in a sheet of your own, given as `CustomCss` (see [[Report Configuration|Report-Configuration]]).
+That sheet comes after the report's own sheets, so its values win. Set the light values on `:root`, and the dark
+values twice, as the token sheet does: on `:root[data-theme="dark"]`, which the script in the page's head sets for a
+reader who picked dark and for a page following a dark system setting, and again on `:root:not([data-theme])` under
+`prefers-color-scheme: dark`, for a copy of the page opened without its scripts. A value set on `:root` alone shows
+in the light theme only.
+
+```css
+:root {
+    --kron-accent: #0b6e4f;
+    --kron-selected: #d7efe5;
+    --kron-selected-ink: #0a5c42;
+}
+:root[data-theme="dark"] {
+    --kron-accent: #5fd0a8;
+    --kron-selected: #17362b;
+    --kron-selected-ink: #a8e6cf;
+}
+@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
+    :root:not([data-theme]) {
+        --kron-accent: #5fd0a8;
+        --kron-selected: #17362b;
+        --kron-selected-ink: #a8e6cf;
+    }
+}
+```
+
+Keep text at 4.5:1 or more on the grounds it sits on (`--kron-card`, `--kron-ground`, `--kron-strip`), in both themes.
+
+A sheet written against 4.x's rules or colours may no longer apply where 5.0.0 changed the markup: the features and
+their steps, the failure diff, the parameter table, the run band, the filter rows and the payload controls. Where it
+still applies, it paints the same colours in both themes. Set the tokens instead.
+[[Migrating to v5: the report|Migrating-to-v5-Report]] lists the classes and functions 5.0.0 took out.
+
+### The violet theme
+
+The Specifications report's default sheet, `Stylesheets.VioletThemeStyleSheet` (the default of
+`HtmlSpecificationsCustomStyleSheet`), is a theme written this way. It sets the report's tokens for the light and the
+dark theme in the three blocks above, adds a few variables of its own (`--violet-card`, `--violet-rail`,
+`--violet-edge`, `--violet-solid`, `--violet-solid-hover`) for its cards and its solid violet, and then gives a short
+list of rules their colours from those variables: the violet cards, the hover edges, and the chosen controls in solid
+violet under white. Set `HtmlSpecificationsCustomStyleSheet` to `null` for the Specifications report in the default
+blue.
+
+## Token reference
+
+Every token, with its value in each theme. The page tokens colour the report itself; the diagram tokens colour what
+the page draws in a diagram.
