 [labs page](Cross-Run-History#in-the-html-460) beside it), and neither does a report generated with no
 ledger: in either, a verdict query matches nothing, without an error.
 
+## Qualifiers (5.0.0)
+
+Three qualifiers narrow a search as the filter rows do: a key, a colon and a value, with no space after the colon.
+
+| Qualifier | Keeps | Example |
+|-----------|-------|---------|
+| `dep:name` | Scenarios that call a dependency whose name holds `name` (`dependency:` is the same key) | `dep:payment` |
+| `duration:` | Scenarios by their own time, compared with a time, a percentile or a range | `duration:>2s` |
+| `is:happy` | Happy paths | `is:happy` |
+
+### Dependencies (`dep:`)
+
+`dep:payment` keeps the scenarios that call a dependency whose name holds `payment`: one of the participants the
+Dependencies row lists for the scenario. Case, spaces and punctuation are ignored on both sides, so
+`dep:orderservice` finds `Order Service` and `order-service`. Quote a name with a space in it
+(`dep:"order service"`), and separate names with commas to keep a scenario that calls any of them
+(`dep:payment,order`).
+
+### Own time (`duration:`)
+
+`duration:` compares a scenario's own time, its recorded duration less the first-call warm-up it paid, as the
+Duration row does ([[Why is my first scenario slow?|Why-Is-My-First-Scenario-Slow]]):
+
+- **An operator and a time**: `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=` or `=`, as in `duration:<500ms`. With no operator the time is a
+  minimum, so `duration:2s` is `duration:>=2s`. `=` matches a time within half a millisecond.
+- **A range**, both ends included: `duration:1s..5s`.
+- **A time** is a number with `ms`, `s`, `m` or `min` after it, a decimal point allowed (`duration:>1.5s`); a number
+  alone is seconds. `p50`, `p90`, `p95` and `p99` are this report's percentiles, the times the Duration row's buttons
+  show: `duration:>=p90`.
+
+A scenario with no recorded duration is never kept by `duration:`, and always kept by `!!duration:`.
+
+### Happy paths (`is:happy`)
+
+`is:happy` keeps the scenarios marked as happy paths, the ones the Happy paths filter shows on Only
+([[Tags and Attributes|Tags-and-Attributes]]). `is:happy-path`, `is:happypath` and their plurals are the same.
+
+### How qualifiers combine
+
+- A qualifier stands on its own: at the start of the search, or after a space or `(`.
+- `!!` before a qualifier keeps the scenarios it would leave out: `!!dep:payment`, `!!is:happy`.
+- Qualifiers always narrow. They combine with the rest of the search, and with each other, by AND, whatever operator
+  stands beside them: `order || dep:payment` keeps the scenarios that match `order` and call a payment dependency.
+  Put the alternatives inside one qualifier instead (`dep:payment,order`).
+- Only `dep:`, `dependency:`, `duration:` and `is:` are keys, in any case: `status:400` and `milk:` are text.
+- A qualifier the search cannot read, such as `duration:fast`, `is:sad` or a percentile in a report with no
+  durations, stays in the search as text, and the search field's border turns amber.
+- They are part of the search, so the page's link carries them in `q=`, and Clear All clears them.
+
